{
  "_comment": [
    "A small NSQF corpus in the exact document shape of iism_nsqf_master_data.",
    "Hand-built rather than sampled, so every trap the real feed contains is present",
    "in something small enough to read.",
    "",
    "Field-naming traps, which is how the largest real error happened: a standard",
    "states its level in 'nsqf', a qualification in 'nsqfLevel'; a standard uses",
    "'Sectors'/'Occupation' where a qualification uses 'sectors'/'occupation'; the",
    "model curriculum spells its key 'compulsary'.",
    "",
    "Also present: half-levels, '4' against '4.0', trailing whitespace in titles,",
    "credits of 'TBD', HH:MM durations, grouped elective/optional units, a",
    "superseded QP version, one sectorID under two spellings, an unreadable level,",
    "a blank curriculum unitCode, occupationID reused across sectors, alignedTo in",
    "clean, variant and junk forms, structured minEduQual entry routes, an",
    "assessment blueprint, and a repeated pcID within one standard."
  ],
